            "bruteForceAttack": true,
            "guessesPerSecond": 10000000,
            "requiredCrackSeconds": 31536000,
            "maxTokens": 6,
            "memorabilityBudget": 11
          }
        ]
      },
      "persona": "Hacktivist",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Imani Vale:</b> Whatever you write here, a receptionist has to use it forty times a week. Remediation that ignores that gets quietly worked around, and then everyone blames the staff for the workaround instead of the rule that caused it.\n\nSo the portal credential has to be something a human can carry, and the heavier burden belongs on the service account, where no human has to remember anything at all.",
      "taskInstructions": "A round clears only when every attack meter for that account survives the required time, inside its token slot and memorability limits. Rare, unusual words buy far more resistance per memorability point than leet spellings, digit suffixes, or breach-dump favorites.",
      "taskQuestion": "Forge the replacement credentials.",
      "taskCompleteText": "You matched each replacement to the threat it faces and kept the staff credential practical. Security improves when the control works for the people expected to use it."
    }
